.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-singleton 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-singleton \- Whether a second copy of a task may start in this clone
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten singleton\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Whether a second copy of a task may start in this clone
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-singleton\-acquire(1)
Take a task\*(Aqs lock for a pid, or refuse naming the process that holds it
.TP
batten\-singleton\-release(1)
Drop a task\*(Aqs lock, which its exit trap does and a kill cannot
.TP
batten\-singleton\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
